problem: npm run hatchet-worker failed because flow runner startup imported batch/render.ts, which eagerly imported optional @mariozechner/pi-tui
approach: moved batch op summary formatting into dependency-free src/batch/summary.ts and retargeted runner-events/render imports there so the Hatchet worker path no longer loads TUI code at module import time
failed_paths:
  - considered adding pi-tui as a dependency, but that would mask the import graph issue and broaden packaging scope
verification:
  - npm run build
  - npx vitest run --reporter=dot tests/hatchet-worker-cli.test.ts tests/batch-summary.test.ts
  - timeout 10s npm run hatchet-worker with .envrc sourced; worker reached ready state for pi-agent-flow.runFlow
workflow_learning: when a non-TUI entrypoint fails on optional UI peers, split pure formatting helpers from render modules instead of widening dependencies
related_files:
  - src/batch/summary.ts
  - src/runner-events.ts
  - src/render.ts
  - tests/batch-summary.test.ts
